  "question": {
    "text": "The descending order of acidity for the following carboxylic acid is-<br />(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></math><br />(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math><br />(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math><br />(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math><br />(E) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BrCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math><br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The correct order of acidic strength of the given carboxylic acids will be decided by the stability of their conjugate bases. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> effect of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;group destabilises the carboxylate anion. But the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> effect of halogen substituted methyl group stabilises the carboxylate anion. Higher the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;effect of the halogen substituted methyl group, higher the acidic strength of the corresponding acid.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Correct order of acidic strength is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><munder><mi>COOH</mi><mtext>&#160;(B)&#160;</mtext></munder><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>FCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><munder><mi>COOH</mi><mtext>&#160;(D)&#160;</mtext></munder><mo>&#62;</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi>CICH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></mrow><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></munder><mo>&#62;</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi>BrCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></mrow><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfenced></munder><mo>&#62;</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></mrow><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></munder></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}